  "body": "## What\n\nWith no machine in the document the plasma post's refusal read\n\n> … only a plasma table reads - **no machine is not declared a plasma machine**\n\nThe engine always publishes a `machine` object (empty name when the document\nstates none), so the old `|| \"no machine\"` fallback made the sentence a double\nnegative. It now says:\n\n> … only a plasma table reads - **no machine is stated, so none is declared a\n> plasma machine**\n\nA named non-plasma machine keeps the old wording (`<name> is not declared a\nplasma machine`), and the rotary refusal falls back to \"the machine\" instead of\nan empty subject.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base main` — ok (1 step, `app:plasma_post_refusals::the_post_refuses_what_a_plasma_table_cannot_say`)\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test plasma_post_refusals` — 7 passed\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test plasma_post` — 5 passed\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test conformance` — 6 passed (goldens byte-exact, unchanged)\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings` — clean\n\nThe regression assertion lives in the area's existing test file\n(`plasma_post_refusals.rs`): a mill still names itself, and a machine-less\ndocument says it states none — and never says \"no machine is not declared\".\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No posted NC golden changes: the wording is a refusal (a warning), and\n  `every_builtin_posts_every_golden_byte_exact` still passes.\n- The issue asks for the #926 refusal goldens to be regenerated; #926 is still\n  open and those recorded-stream suites do not exist on main yet, so there is\n  nothing to regenerate here. When #926 lands, its goldens will record this\n  wording.\n\nChangelog: the plasma post's machine-less refusal reads as a sentence again (#998)\nFixes #998\n",
